{
 "name": "Tank cross-section: T-80U turret cheek",
 "category": "armor",
 "description": "Cast turret seen from above: Kontakt-5 in front, then the cheek at ~47 deg to a frontal shot - 98 mm cast outer wall, a 260 mm insert of ~60 mm alumina cylinders in polyurethane (estimates disagree: ceramic cylinders vs cellular polymer), 190 mm cast rear wall. Estimates vs long rods 630-860 mm with Kontakt-5. Reconstruction from public sources (Tankograd, Below The Turret Ring, Zaloga/Wikipedia, forum analyses); real tank armour is secret. Armour amount = public protection estimate / mass efficiency (NERA ~1.3-1.5, Soviet arrays ~1.17). The explosive inside ERA is an empty gap until explosives are added, and the model under-represents NERA breaking long rods - so a full simulation is penetrated more easily than the real armour; the Tank check uses the estimates. 2D slice.",
